English Version

FinxWork is licensed under a modified version of the Apache License 2.0 (full
text attached below), with the following additional conditions. In the event of
any conflict between these additional conditions and the Apache License 2.0,
these additional conditions shall prevail.

1. Commercial Use and Cases Requiring Written Authorization

FinxWork may be used free of charge by individuals and organizations (including
self-hosted deployment and internal business use within a single organization);
however, a prior written commercial license must be obtained from FinxWork if
any of the following conditions apply:

  a. Multi-tenant and Hosted Services:
     Unless explicitly authorized by FinxWork in writing, you may not use the
     FinxWork source code or compiled artifacts to operate a multi-tenant
     environment, or to provide SaaS, cloud hosting, or hosted multi-user
     services to external third parties (whether paid or free).
     - Tenant Definition: Within the context of FinxWork, a "Tenant" refers to
       an independent workspace, account space, or isolated data and runtime
       boundary serving a distinct external individual, enterprise, or customer
       entity.

  b. Prohibition on Sale, Resale, and Commercial Bundling:
     Without prior written authorization from FinxWork, you may not directly or
     indirectly sell, rent, lease, sublicense for a fee, or resell FinxWork
     (including its source code, binary installers, modified versions, or
     derivative works), nor bundle or pre-install it with paid software or
     hardware devices, or offer it as a primary deliverable of paid deployment,
     installation, or managed-operation services for third parties.

  c. LOGO and Copyright Information:
     When using FinxWork's user interface or brand assets (including
     `apps/desktop`, `apps/chrome-extension`, `assets/brand/`, and built or
     distributed artifacts thereof), you may not remove, obscure, or modify the
     FinxWork LOGO, product name, or copyright and attribution notices.
     (This UI LOGO restriction does not apply to headless CLI or backend-only
     uses of FinxWork that do not expose FinxWork's graphical interface,
     provided that copyright and license notices in the source and distributed
     artifacts remain intact.)

2. Redistribution and Derivative Works

You may distribute FinxWork or its modified versions in accordance with this
license, provided that all externally distributed modified versions and
derivative works remain subject to this license (including all additional
conditions above). You may not relicense them under other terms, nor remove or
weaken these additional conditions.

3. Contributions

By submitting a contribution (including code, documentation, or translations)
to this project, you represent that you have the right to submit it, and you
agree that:
  a. FinxWork may adjust the license agreement of this project (to be stricter
     or more relaxed) as deemed necessary;
  b. Your contributed code may be used by FinxWork for commercial purposes,
     including cloud service operations and granting commercial licenses to
     third parties.

4. Miscellaneous
  a. For commercial licensing, white-label/OEM authorization, multi-tenant SaaS
     licensing, or commercial distribution inquiries, please email
     yipengfei329@gmail.com.
  b. Third-party open-source components, fonts, models, and dependencies
     included in this software remain under their own respective licenses.
  c. This license is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China.
     In case of any discrepancy between the Chinese and English versions, the
     Chinese version prevails.

